From 871f96509962efb24d048de8c9b47fb4168b4244 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Leva <120221487+Levaj2000@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:51:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(audit): add the OCSF audit sink as a reference
 plugin

Adapt the imported crate to this tree: workspace member, workspace
dependencies, the lint set, edition 2024, and the file header and comment
conventions. The record format and every hashed byte are unchanged; the
three conformance vectors next to the crate reproduce byte for byte.

What changed in the adaptation:

- One host. The crate selected its engine by a Cargo feature; here it
  depends on praxis-policy-core alone, so the feature pair, the host alias
  module and its shims are gone. The denying-step violation is read from
  PluginAction::Denied / DenyIgnored directly and the output digest from
  DecisionLog::output_hash, which drops the payload parameter from
  ocsf::apply_decision.
- Dependencies from the workspace table. p256 joins the table (ecdsa, pem,
  pkcs8); base64 follows the major the builtins declare.
- Lints. No unwrap, expect or Value indexing in library code: the
  canonicalizer uses Display, the chain state recovers a poisoned lock,
  and the attestation members are inserted through the map. Tests and
  examples carry the same scoped allows as the existing reference
  plugins.
- Edition 2024. provenance_demo resolved its demo keys through the env
  secret backend with std::env::set_var, which is unsafe in this edition;
  it now writes them to a scratch directory and resolves through the file
  backend. Same bytes, same digests.
- Comments and docs explain the code, not its history, and every public
  item is documented.

Also registers the plugin in the README layout note and gives the
auditing guide a second sink block for kind: audit/ocsf.

Verified on the pinned toolchain: make lint, make test, make doc,
cargo deny check, cargo check --workspace --all-targets with and without
--all-features; 35 tests; emit_sample, decision_sink_demo and
provenance_demo byte-identical to their vectors; panic_drive lands the
driven panic on gw-1:decision at stream_seq 0 with status_code
plugin_panic.

Source: Levaj2000/AI-Identity at 395d64ed8bea695896af1557e530b0065145f593, integrations/cpex-ocsf-audit.
